    <section class="rise-fall" id="timeline" aria-labelledby="timeline-title">
      <h2 class="profile-section-title" id="timeline-title">Timeline</h2>
      <ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">12th century</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sheikh-adi-ibn-musafir">Sheikh Adi ibn Musafir</a> settles in the valley of Lalish, unites the scattered Yazidi tribes and returns their ancient temple to them</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1246</span><span class="rf-text">Badr al-Din Lu’lu, ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosul">Mosul</a>, has Sheikh Hasan, the leader who had consolidated the Yazidi community, killed</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1414</span><span class="rf-text">A joint army of neighbouring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a> Kurdish tribes ransacks Lalish</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1566</span><span class="rf-text">The Ottoman Sheikh al-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> issues <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatwa">fatwas</a> legitimising the killing of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazidis">Yazidis</a> and the enslavement and sale of Yazidi women</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1640</span><span class="rf-text">An Ottoman army under Melek Ahmed Pasha storms Mount <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sinjar">Sinjar</a>, where 3,060 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazidis">Yazidis</a> are killed</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1832</span><span class="rf-text">The forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mir-muhammad-kor">Muhammad Pasha of Rawanduz</a> massacre the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazidis">Yazidis</a> of Sheikhan, enslave thousands and execute those who refuse <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1915</span><span class="rf-text">During the Armenian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a> many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazidis">Yazidis</a> are killed, and others flee from Van, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kars">Kars</a> and Bazîd to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-caucasus">Transcaucasia</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">2014</span><span class="rf-text">The Islamic State captures <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sinjar">Sinjar</a> and begins the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazidis">Yazidis</a>: over 5,000 are killed and thousands of women and girls forced into sexual <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a></span></li></ol>
    </section>

